    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d450-a2">

                <pb facs="0806" n="710" xml:id="pg710"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 127.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Moore to Mr.
                            Turner.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1874-06-06"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 6,
                    1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am in receipt of your dispatch stating,
                    for the information of his excellency the President of the republic, that the
                    United States ship of war Congress is now at anchor in this harbor, &amp;c.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to reply that 12 o’clock m. has been selected as the hour for an
                    interchange of a national salute; and that the President will be pleased to
                    receive you, the commander of the Congress, and the officers of his staff, at 11
                    o’clock a.m. With assurances of profound respect and esteem, I have,
                    &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. E. MOORE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
